### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 0. Login to get token (run this first, or whenever token expires)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "duplicate-test@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("authToken", response.body.token);
%}

### 1. Create an API key (happy path)
# Expect: 201 Created, response body includes id, apiKey (raw, usable), createdAt
# IMPORTANT: copy the "apiKey" value from this response now — it will never be shown again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/merchants/me/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 2. Create a second API key for the same merchant
# Expect: 201 Created, a DIFFERENT id and apiKey than request 1 — confirms multiple keys per merchant works
POST {{baseUrl}}/merchants/me/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 3. Attempt to create an API key without a token
# Expect: 401 Unauthorized (filter chain should block this before reaching the controller)
POST {{baseUrl}}/merchants/me/api-keys

### 4. Attempt to create an API key with a malformed/garbage token
# Expect: 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/merchants/me/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer this.is.not.a.valid.jwt